OSKit Arch — aarch64 Virtual Memory
===================================

aarch64 page-table helpers and the physical page allocator. Pairs
with `mmu.s` (identity map + MMU enable at boot) and `vm_asm.s`
(TTBR0 / TLB wrappers). The interface mirrors
`oskit/arch/x86_64/vm.lsysl` so kernel code can import from
`oskit.arch` regardless of target.

At boot the MMU is already on with a 1GB/1GB identity map covering
RAM and the MMIO region; this module provides the read/write
primitives for future per-process page tables.

    module oskit.arch

    import oskit.config.{PAGE_SIZE}

Page tables emitted by `mmu.s`.

    extern l0_table: byte

Hardware page-table operations (vm_asm.s).

    extern vm_set_ptbr(addr: u64)
    extern vm_flush_tlb()
    extern vm_get_ptbr() -> u64

Kernel page-table base, captured on first call so later code can
route around it (e.g. building per-process tables that clone a
kernel-half range). On aarch64 this is simply the TTBR0 we set up
in `mmu_init`.

    var kernel_ttbr0: u64 = 0

    kernel_ptbr() -> u64
        if kernel_ttbr0 == 0
            kernel_ttbr0 = u64(i64(&l0_table))
        kernel_ttbr0

aarch64 descriptor encoding bits we'll need repeatedly.

    val PTE_VALID: i64 = 1          // bit 0 — valid
    val PTE_TABLE: i64 = 2          // bit 1 — table (vs block/page)
    val PTE_PAGE:  i64 = 2          // bit 1 — page (at L3)
    val PTE_AF:    i64 = 0x400      // bit 10 — access flag

Mask for extracting the output address from a level 1/2/3 descriptor.

    val PTE_ADDR_MASK: i64 = 0x0000FFFFFFFFF000

Raw 64-bit entry read/write. All aarch64 descriptors are 64-bit.

    vm_write_pte64(addr: u64, pte: i64)
        var p: *i64 = *i64(addr)
        *p = pte

    vm_read_pte64(addr: u64) -> i64
        var p: *i64 = *i64(addr)
        *p

Physical page allocator — bump + free list, same shape as the
x86_64 version. RAM starts at 0x40000000 on QEMU virt; pool sits
between the kernel image and the top of our 1GB identity map.

    val PAGE_POOL_END: u64 = 0x80000000

    extern _heap_start: byte

    var page_pool_next: u64 = 0
    var page_pool_init = false
    var page_free_list: u64 = 0

    page_alloc() -> u64
        if !page_pool_init
            var base = u64(i64(&_heap_start))
            val aligned = (base + u64(PAGE_SIZE - 1)) & ~u64(PAGE_SIZE - 1)
            page_pool_next = aligned
            page_pool_init = true
        if page_free_list != 0
            val page = page_free_list
            var next: *i64 = *i64(page)
            page_free_list = u64(*next)
            return page
        if page_pool_next >= PAGE_POOL_END
            return 0
        val page = page_pool_next
        page_pool_next += u64(PAGE_SIZE)
        page

    page_free(addr: u64)
        var p: *i64 = *i64(addr)
        *p = i64(page_free_list)
        page_free_list = addr

    page_alloc_zero() -> u64
        val page = page_alloc()
        if page != 0
            // Clear the freshly-allocated page byte-by-byte. Slow but
            // one-line; replace with a memset/DC ZVA helper once the
            // arch has a proper memset.
            var p: *byte = *byte(page)
            var i = 0
            while i < PAGE_SIZE
                p[i] = 0
                i += 1
        page
